 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The veterinarian directory answers which specialties a veterinarian holds. Staff also ask the inverse. The clinic therefore publishes a specialty directory: every specialty it knows, under the name it is stored by, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. A veterinarian is shown by full name, first name before last name. One holding no specialty appears nowhere, because the page lists specialties rather than the whole roster `[REQ-VET-003]`. Every specialty is shown on a single page, and the page has an address of its own that nothing links to `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then each is listed under its stored name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each of them is shown by first name followed by last name, such as "Helen Leary".
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given more specialties than fill one screen, when the directory is opened, then all of them are on that one page, with no paging.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the veterinarian directory or any other page, when it is rendered, then it carries no link to the specialty directory.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the supported languages, when the page's wording is checked, then every piece of it is present in each of them (`REQ-LANG-002`).
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+2. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty appears under each of them.
+3. Specialties, and the veterinarians within each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+4. A clinic that knows no specialties yields a page that renders and lists none.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
